# Auto commit and push

After making project changes, commit them and `git push` to the tracked remote. Do not ask for approval first.

- Include relevant untracked source files; never commit secrets (`.env`, tokens, live `config/settings.yaml`, `config/strategy.yaml`, credential files).
- Use a concise 1–2 sentence commit message focused on why.
- Do not force-push, skip hooks, amend published commits, or change git config.
- If there is nothing to commit, skip the commit; still push if the branch is ahead of origin.
